# Veltrix Custom License

Copyright (c) 2026 Rayler_Laurent

This license applies to Veltrix and its original files, unless otherwise stated.

## 1. Permissions

The following uses are permitted:

- **Modification:** You are free to modify, edit, and create derivative works based on Veltrix.
- **Redistribution of Modified Versions:** You may distribute and publish modified versions and derivative works, including commercially.
- **Modpacks:** You may include Veltrix in public or private modpacks, including commercial modpacks.
- **Commercial Use:** Commercial use of Veltrix and its derivatives is permitted.
- **Source Code:** Publishing the source code of modified versions is optional.
- **Licensing of Derivatives:** You may choose any license for your own modified versions or derivative works, provided that you respect the rights and conditions applicable to the original Veltrix materials.

## 2. Attribution

When distributing Veltrix as part of a modpack, or distributing a modified version or derivative work, you must:

- Credit the original author: **Rayler_Laurent**.
- Provide a link to the official Veltrix project page.

Modified versions and derivatives must clearly indicate that they are unofficial and must not be presented as the official Veltrix release.

The use of the Veltrix name and logo is permitted for derivative works, provided that the derivative nature of the project is clearly indicated and it is not confused with the official release.

Credit for individual contributors will generally be provided when their work is incorporated into the official project. However, if a contributor requests not to be credited, their request will be respected.

## 3. Restrictions on Unmodified Redistribution

Redistributing the original, unmodified Veltrix files as a standalone download is prohibited without prior permission from the author.

If you wish to redistribute the unmodified version independently, you must contact the author in advance and provide:

- The intended purpose and reason for redistribution.
- A description of how the files will be used.
- A link to the page or platform where the files will be distributed.

Redistribution is permitted only after receiving explicit approval from the author.

This restriction does not apply to including Veltrix in modpacks, which is permitted under Section 1.

## 4. Contributions and Official Integration

### 4.1 Contributions Submitted by Others

Anyone may submit features, code, or other contributions for consideration in the official Veltrix project.

By submitting a contribution for official integration, the contributor grants the author permission to incorporate the submitted contribution into the official Veltrix project.

The author may review, modify, adapt, or reject any submitted contribution before integration.

### 4.2 Changes to Integrated Contributions

Once a contribution has been approved and integrated into the official project, the author of Veltrix may freely:

- Modify or adapt the contributed feature.
- Improve or refactor its implementation.
- Combine it with other features.
- Change or replace its implementation.
- Remove the feature from the official project.

The original contributor retains the copyright to their contribution unless they explicitly transfer those rights to the author through a separate agreement.

Permission to integrate a contribution does not, by itself, constitute a transfer of copyright ownership.

### 4.3 Official Invitations and External Projects

The author may contact creators of addons, extensions, or derivative projects and request permission to:

- Incorporate their features into the official Veltrix project.
- Link to or introduce their projects on the official Veltrix website.

Such use requires the creator's explicit permission.

Any copyright ownership remains with the original creator unless it is explicitly transferred to the author through a separate agreement.

## 5. No Warranty and Limitation of Liability

Veltrix is provided **"AS IS"**, without warranties of any kind, whether express or implied.

Use of Veltrix is entirely at your own risk.

The author provides no warranty or guarantee regarding the functionality, compatibility, stability, or safety of Veltrix or any modified versions or derivative works.

The author shall not be held liable for any damages, losses, data loss, or other issues arising from the use, modification, distribution, or inability to use Veltrix or its derivatives, to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law.

The author takes no responsibility for modified versions or derivative works created or distributed by third parties.

## 6. License Violations and Enforcement

If a violation of this license is identified, the following procedure will generally apply:

1. The author will verify the suspected violation.
2. The person responsible will be contacted and asked to correct the violation, stop distribution, or remove the infringing files or content.
3. If the person complies with the request, the author will generally treat the first violation as resolved without further action.
4. If the person refuses to comply, the author may consider further action, including legal action.

The author reserves the right to take immediate action in cases of serious, malicious, or repeated violations.

## 7. License Changes and Updates

The author reserves the right to update or modify this license at any time.

- New versions of Veltrix released after a license update will be subject to the updated license.
- Previously released versions will remain subject to the license that accompanied them at the time of their release.
- Changes to this license will not retroactively revoke permissions already granted under an earlier version.

## 8. Contact

For permissions, questions, or other inquiries regarding this license, please contact the original author through the official Veltrix project page.

